      "content": "<h3>4. Constructors and the 0.75 / 16 defaults</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Signature:</strong> <code>new HashSet&lt;&gt;();  new HashSet&lt;&gt;(int cap);  new HashSet&lt;&gt;(int cap, float load);  new HashSet&lt;&gt;(Collection c)</code></li>\n<li><strong>Returns:</strong> a set</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> O(1) / O(n)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>For freshers:</strong> <code>new HashSet&lt;&gt;()</code> creates <code>new HashMap&lt;&gt;()</code> (capacity 16, load factor 0.75). The copy constructor sizes the map as <code>max((int)(c.size() / .75f) + 1, 16)</code> so that copying does not trigger a resize.</p>\n<p><strong>For experienced developers:</strong> Because the backing map has lazy allocation, the array of buckets is created only on the first <code>add</code>.</p>",
